{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Now you will see.</b> Rashi explained that the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: I tested Abraham and he did not harbor doubts, but you have harbored doubts. But in fact, even though Abraham said ״במה אדע״, this is not harboring doubts; rather, Abraham said to the Holy One, blessed be He: By what merit shall I know that I will inherit the land? And He said to Him, may He be exalted: ״קחה לי עגלה משולשת״ — that is, by the merit of the sacrifices you will inherit the land."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:43.401328457Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}